{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_1004064348#1_2084573064","relevance":3,"reason":"The BrightHub Education article is directly about the importance of teacher self-assessment as the first step in a teacher improvement plan. It explains that reviewing instruction helps teachers identify areas for improvement, respond to concepts students struggled with, and become more effective teachers.","learned":"Teacher self-assessment helps teachers see where they can improve, address student struggles, and become more effective in teaching and classroom management."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q557","reason":"The self-reflection/self-assessment query produced a dedicated grade-3 result; continue through it to find more direct evidence about why teachers should review instruction."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q557"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_978019507#4_1907983876","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q557","rank":2,"snippet":"email or messaging, or upload to cloud storage like Google Drive or a video management system. - Share with your coach for feedback, <cover>improvement and evaluation - Send great student learning moments to their parents - Model how to conduct a lesson for one of your teammates Start with a Whole Class Audio System Whole class audio systems provide even distribution of sound so all students hear, and understand instruction. They are the foundation for the Activate System, which includes microphone (s), Pods and Activate Station. Redcat Access Topcat Access 955 Access \" , \"segment\": \"Capturing Video Capture and share audio and video of critical teaching and learning moments. Activate the power of video capture in your mobile device Video capture is powerful and accessible Video is becoming an important tool in the classroom. Video and photo capabilities in our everyday devices are rapidly increasing teacher's use of video capture for: - Self-reflection on their own instruction - Evidence of student engagement and understanding - Classroom observation and coaching - Exchanging teaching ideas with peers Activate lets teachers </cover>sync up the audio from anywhere in the class The Activate App overcomes a device's inability to capture quality audio beyond a "}}
