{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_6250596#5_10391822","relevance":2,"reason":"The result supports the information need by explaining that coaching, collaboration, and reflection help teachers connect professional development to student learning and improve instructional practice. However, it is mainly about professional development and continuous improvement plans, not dedicated to why teachers should always review their own instruction.","learned":"Structured reflection and collaboration help teachers examine the impact of practice on student learning, improve instructional practice, and align improvement efforts with school goals."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"importance of reflective practice\" teachers (+ teaching instruction) (+ improve learning students))","reason":"Search for sources explicitly about the importance of reflective practice for teachers, likely to provide dedicated evidence on why teachers should continually review instruction."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"importance of reflective practice\" teachers (+ teaching instruction) (+ improve learning students))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_233959022#8_620129047","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q562","rank":1,"snippet":"<cover>Importance of Reflective Practice in Continously Improving the Quality of Service Provided. Ctls Level3 Essay Develop a Workplace Learning Environment Working Together for the Benefit of Children and Young People ‘Aha’ Moments – Reasons for Emergence and Their Implications in Improving the Efficacy of Coaching Effective Teaching Strategies Cyp Core 3.5 2.1 1.1 Explain How To Recognise And Build On The Strength Of A Child And Young Children Essay Multi Agency Working/Partnership Working in Social Care Child Care Unit 25 Level 3 Ta \" , \"segment\": \"Positive communication is very important as this can help build a Childs interaction skills, self esteem and confidence. It’s vital you always have eye contact with that child, and allow them to finish what they are saying. In order to boost their self esteem a child should always be praised, this will make them feel more confident and willing to try. Adapting the environment to help children with their speech and language needs can be done by using visual signs that children can understand, for example you could label the home corner, dress up area, book corner and so on. Read More Multi Agency Working/Partnership </cover>"}}
