{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_913400549#1_1885626115","relevance":2,"reason":"The result supports the information need by saying professional learning communities enhance teacher reflection on instructional practices and student outcomes, allowing teachers to share best practices and improve learning and student achievement. However, it is primarily about PLC benefits rather than a document dedicated to why teachers should always review their instruction.","learned":"Teacher review/reflection can be strengthened through PLCs, where educators examine instructional practice and student outcomes, share best practices, and improve learning and achievement."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"benefits of teacher reflection\" (+ instruction teaching practice) (+ students learning improve))","reason":"Search directly for documents about the benefits of teacher reflection, which should be more dedicated to why teachers should review their instruction."}}
