{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"reflective practice\" \"professional development\" teachers (+ improve teaching learning) students)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_506102743#3_1032621383","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q565","rank":1,"snippet":"What happens after I take the exam? What happens if I don’t pass the exam? Praxis (5264) Principles of Learning and Teaching: 7-12 STUDY GUIDE Praxis II Principles of Learning and Teaching: Grades 7–12 Study Materials \" , \"segment\": \"Student development and the learning process, students as diverse learners, and student motivation and the learning environment. Instructional Process: Planning instruction, instructional strategies, questioning techniques, and communication techniques. Assessment: Assessment and evaluation strategies and assessment tools. Professional Development, Leadership, and Community: <cover>Professional development practices and resources, research, views, ideas, and debates on teaching practices, reflective practice for professional growth, school support personnel who assist students, teachers, </cover>and families, teachers and schools as educational leaders in the community, developing collaborative relationships, and implications of major legislation with regard to students and teachers. Analysis of Instructional Scenarios: Related to two case histories on the topics of students as learners, instructional process, assessment, and professional development, leadership, and community. What is the most convenient way to register for the exam?\" , \"start_char\": 1511.000000 , \"title\": \"Praxis II Principles of Learning & Teaching: 7–12 Practice Test ("}}
