{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1309807022#21_2717505203","relevance":2,"reason":"The BookWidgets result is dedicated to becoming a reflective teacher and provides reflection prompts for reviewing teaching abilities, lessons, assessment, classroom management, and professional development. However, the snippet focuses more on how to reflect than directly explaining why teachers should always review instruction.","learned":"Reflection-in-teaching resources often frame instructional review through questions about lessons, student understanding, assessment, classroom management, and professional development."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1309807022#21_2717505203","reason":"The article title suggests a dedicated reflective-teaching guide; the full document may contain direct reasons and benefits that would justify a higher relevance judgment or reveal additional evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1309807022#21_2717505203"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1309807022#21_2717505203","document":"How to become a reflective teacher - The complete guide for reflection in teaching - BookWidgets ... How to become a reflective teacher - The complete guide for reflection in teaching How to become a reflective teacher - The complete guide for reflection in teaching What is reflective teaching? 10 Ways to reflect on your teaching 1. Use exit slips 2. Include reflection in your lesson plan 3. Use a teacher reflection survey 4. An extra pair of teacher’s eyes 5. Use a reflective journal 6. Videotape your teaching 7. One-minute reflections 8. Reflection practice checklist 9. Create a teacher moodboard 10. Best and worst teacher analyses 20 reflection questions for teachers Reflection questions to ask with students Reflection question about assessment and grading Reflection questions about classroom management Reflection questions for teachers’ professional development  ... Get your heads together. As a group, identify if any of these “themes” you wrote down occur several times. Make a top 5 of the group. Now you have a list with qualities, skills or attitudes you want to adopt or get out the way as a teacher yourself. 20 reflection questions for teachers In the reflection approaches above, you’ll already find some reflection resources for teachers. And of course, there’s more. I listed some other important question prompts you can ask yourself when reflecting on your teaching abilities. The reflection questions are divided in different categories: Reflection questions to ask with students Did this lesson help you understand other lessons better? Why?","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
