{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1309807022#21_2717505203","relevance":2,"reason":"The full BookWidgets document is a guide to becoming a reflective teacher and gives tools and questions for reviewing lessons, teaching abilities, assessment, classroom management, and professional development. It is useful but still more focused on how to reflect than on directly answering why teachers should always review their instruction.","learned":"Reflective-teaching guides support review through exit slips, reflection surveys, peer observation, journals, video, checklists, and questions about student understanding and teaching abilities."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"benefits of reflective teaching\" teachers (+ students learning instruction improve))","reason":"Search directly for the phrase 'benefits of reflective teaching' to find dedicated sources that explain why teachers should review their instruction and how it improves teaching and student learning."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"benefits of reflective teaching\" teachers (+ students learning instruction improve))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_453712018#2_911258629","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q567","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_453712018#2_911258629\" , \"end_char\": 2291.000000 , \"headings\": \"12 Benefits of Reflective Teaching and Learning 12 Benefits of Reflective Teaching and <cover>Learning Benefits of Reflective Teaching For Teachers</cover>1. Professional Growth 2. Enhance Innovation 3. Facilitate Teaching 4. Boost Teacher-Student Relationship 5. Make Lessons More Lively and Interesting 6. Enhance Problem Solving 7. Boost Classroom Democracy Benefits of Reflective Learning For Students 8. Improve Student Performance 9. Boost Engagement in Class 10. Develop Critical Thinking and Coping Skills 11. Enhance Student Motivation 12. Improve Overall Effectiveness Related Questions \" , \"segment\": \"If you are a teacher, tutor, lecturer, or teaching assistant (TA) who wants to improve their performance or liven up a class session, this article is for you. Getting started is rather easy: you only need to show some level of commitment and willingness to engage your mind, analyse previous sessions and look for ways to improve on your weak points. Let’s get started. Benefits of Reflective Teaching For Teachers Teachers benefit from reflective teaching practices in a variety of ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_453712018#0_911254408","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
