{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_453712018#8_911269651","relevance":3,"reason":"This segment is from the dedicated article '12 Benefits of Reflective Teaching and Learning' and directly explains why teachers should review instruction: reflective teaching uses needs assessment, helps teachers recognize when methods fall short, and encourages research, networking, and adopting innovative teaching techniques to improve practice.","learned":"Reviewing instruction helps teachers identify ineffective methods, assess needs, keep current with innovative techniques, and improve practice through research and collaboration."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"reflective teaching\" \"student outcomes\" teachers (+ evaluate adjust improve) (+ pedagogy instruction))","reason":"Search for distinct sources linking reflective teaching to evaluating and adjusting instruction or pedagogy to improve student outcomes."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"reflective teaching\" \"student outcomes\" teachers (+ evaluate adjust improve) (+ pedagogy instruction))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_421266880#0_779506295","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q568","rank":2,"snippet":"of comforting cyclicality. While curriculum evolves, the fundamentals of many subjects and age-based learning expectations vary little over time. As a result, you may enjoy the familiarity of teaching many of the same lesson plans year after year. When you fall into a rhythm—a comforting habit of exercises, assignments, and processes­—it can become easy to overlook the importance of self-reflection. Could there be a new, more effective approach to teaching the fundamentals of the periodic table? Could a grammar lesson be improved to produce better concept application? Could you engage with students more effectively if you incorporated more group work into your instruction? <cover>Reflective teaching is an academic style in which teachers regularly self-assess their performance, their teaching style, methodology, and pedagogy, evolving their approach over time to produce optimal student outcomes. The reflective approach requires teachers to take time to evaluate </cover>and adjust their style. What follows are three benefits of reflecting teaching.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Three Benefits of Reflective Teaching | PLS Classes\" , \"url\": \"https://plsclasses.com/three-benefits-of-reflective-teaching\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_421266880#1_779508083","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"29/50"}}
