{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q572"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_74228304#5_144022812","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q572","rank":8,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_74228304#5_144022812\" , \"end_char\": 4856.000000 , \"headings\": \"Statewide Assessments Statewide Assessments Overview Understanding Student Assessment \" , \"segment\": \"Students and their parents use assessment results to check mastery of key learning targets; Teachers use <cover>formative assessment practices and interim/benchmark assessments in the classroom to identify gaps in student learning and adjust instruction; Teachers </cover>and administrators use summative assessment results to review learning patterns annually, to determine systems-level changes that might be required from year-to-year; State and local leaders use summative assessment results to make important policy decisions, like where and how to invest in Oregon schools and how to hold schools accountable for the outcomes of those investments. Help us blaze a better trail Let us know how we can improve this page I'd like to submit a/an Idea/Suggestion Problem Comment How can we make this page more helpful? 250 characters remaining Note: Please do not provide personal information (e.g. address, social security numbers, etc.) No, Thanks Submit\" , \"start_char\""}}
